+Single-planet date/identity aliases no longer select an adopted epoch after the
+absence-evidence stage. They remain intact in the JSON and CSV candidate lists;
+the final status is `planet_epoch_not_identifiable`, its selected matches and
+epoch are empty, and no unmatched-planet constellation is projected onto the
+image. The PDF nevertheless reports the strongest retained blind candidate's
+date, local positional uncertainty and residual as explicitly unconfirmed
+single-planet evidence, separately from any fixed-metadata match. This preserves
+the temporal information without making an independently unsupported identity
+or epoch claim. Conditional multi-planet candidates retain the measured and
+predicted overlays.
 
